                                "sense_id": "da8f76e6-79ed-34e7-a40f-bf4ae93b0149",
                                "text": "When a horse becomes blown, on approaching a fence, you should pause for a second, and turn him round: it will greatly relieve him, and you stand a much better chance of getting over: and indeed, it is generally preferable to turn the horse round at a rasper, or large jump."
